          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "As \\( n\\to\\infty \\) the estimate converges to \\( \\displaystyle\\int_0^4(0.4x^{2}+1)\\,dx \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — The Fundamental Theorem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Part 1: \\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\displaystyle\\int_a^x f(t)\\,dt=f(x) \\). Part 2: \\( \\displaystyle\\int_a^b f=F(b)-F(a) \\). Use <strong>\\( u \\)-substitution</strong> to reverse the chain rule, and Riemann sums to approximate area.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Power rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int x^{n}dx=\\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "FTC",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int_a^b f=F(b)-F(a) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "u-substitution",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int f(g)g'\\,dx \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Accumulation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int_a^b f \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\int_0^2 3x^{2}\\,dx \\).</p>\\[ \\big[x^{3}\\big]_0^2=8. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — FTC Part 1 &amp; 2",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>If \\(g(x)=\\int_0^x\\sin(t^2)\\,dt\\), find \\(g'(x)\\) and evaluate \\(\\int_1^3(2x-x^2)\\,dx\\).</p><p>FTC Part 1: \\(g'(x)=\\sin(x^2)\\).</p>\\[\\int_1^3(2x-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[x^2-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_1^3=\\left(9-9\\right)-\\left(1-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=0-\\frac{2}{3}=-\\frac{2}{3}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Evaluate \\(\\displaystyle\\int\\frac{3x^2}{x^3+1}\\,dx\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Let \\(u=x^3+1\\), \\(du=3x^2\\,dx\\). Integral \\(=\\int\\dfrac{du}{u}=\\ln|u|+c=\\ln|x^3+1|+c\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
